---
import Icon from '@/components/Icon.astro';
---

<div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="wrench" /> Structured Methodology</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[2] text-text2"
  >
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Identify the Problem</strong> — Gather info, question users, check logs,
      try to replicate
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Establish a Theory</strong> — Most probable cause first (layer-by-layer,
      bottom-up)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Test the Theory</strong> — If confirmed, proceed. If not, re-theorize
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Establish a Plan</strong> — Plan the fix, assess impact, schedule if needed
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Implement the Solution</strong> — Make the change, escalate if necessary
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Verify Full Functionality</strong> — Confirm fix and check for new issues
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-text">Document Findings</strong> — Root cause, steps taken, lessons learned
    </li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> Can't Communicate Across VLANs</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Verify VLAN config (show vlan brief)</li><li>
      Check trunk allowed VLANs (show interfaces trunk)
    </li><li>Confirm IP addresses and subnets match</li><li>
      Verify inter-VLAN routing is configured
    </li><li>Check ACLs blocking traffic (show access-lists)</li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> Interface Down / Flapping</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Check physical cables and connections</li><li>
      show interface &lt;intf&gt; — look for errors, CRC, resets
    </li><li>Try shutdown / no shutdown</li><li>Check speed/duplex mismatch (both sides)</li><li>
      Verify SFP/transceiver compatibility
    </li><li>Check for port-security violations</li><li>
      Default the port to reset all config: default interface &lt;intf&gt; — then reconfigure from
      scratch
    </li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> No Internet / WAN Down</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Ping default gateway, then upstream</li><li>
      Check NAT translations (show ip nat translations)
    </li><li>Verify default route exists (show ip route)</li><li>
      Check ISP-facing interface status
    </li><li>Verify DNS resolution (nslookup)</li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> DHCP Not Working</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Verify DHCP pool config (show run | section dhcp)</li><li>
      Check excluded addresses aren't overlapping the pool
    </li><li>Verify ip helper-address if DHCP server is remote</li><li>
      Confirm client interface is up and in correct VLAN
    </li><li>Check DHCP bindings (show ip dhcp binding)</li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> Slow Network / High Latency</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Check interface utilization (show interfaces)</li><li>
      Look for CRC errors, collisions, drops
    </li><li>Verify duplex settings (full duplex expected)</li><li>
      Check for broadcast storms (show interfaces counters)
    </li><li>Monitor bandwidth with SNMP/NetFlow</li><li>
      Verify QoS policies if VoIP affected
    </li><li>Check service-policy drops: show policy-map interface &lt;intf&gt;</li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> OSPF Neighbor Not Forming</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Verify interfaces are in correct area (show ip ospf interface)</li><li>
      Check hello/dead timers match on both sides
    </li><li>Verify subnet masks match</li><li>Check area type matches (stub, NSSA)</li><li>
      Verify authentication matches
    </li><li>Check MTU (must match for adjacency)</li>
  </ol>
</div><div class="panel">
  <h3><Icon name="magnifying-glass" /> QoS / Service Policy Issues</h3><ol
    class="list-decimal pl-[20px] text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-text2"
  >
    <li>Confirm policy applied: show run interface &lt;intf&gt; | include service-policy</li><li>
      View live counters and drops per class: show policy-map interface &lt;intf&gt;
    </li><li>Check for queue tail-drops or WRED drops in the output direction</li><li>
      Verify class-map match conditions are correct: show class-map
    </li><li>Confirm correct policy-map is attached: show run | section service-policy</li><li>
      Check DSCP/CoS markings on ingress traffic: show mls qos interface &lt;intf&gt;
    </li><li>Reset counters: remove service-policy, re-apply, observe fresh counts</li><li>
      Verify DSCP-to-queue mappings: show mls qos maps dscp-output-q
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>
